        <briefdescription>
<para>Generic logical <bold>and</bold> operation, for two or more operands. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>First_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the first operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Second_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type of the second operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Rest_T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Types of the other operands, if any.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>first</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>First operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>second</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Second operand. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>rest</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The other operands, if any. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Constraints</title><para>Enabled only if each operand satisfies <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1checkable" kindref="compound">extension::checkable</ref></computeroutput>, as for <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>An object that evaluates to true if all the operand expressions are true.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-logical-functions_1ga0a385c59a2f7d3c4cfef77d2d3b4f3d6" kindref="member">all_of</ref></computeroutput> function template provides a generic logical conjunction for any expression types. It constructs a <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1and__op" kindref="compound">detail::and_op</ref></computeroutput> logical conjunction object, which evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if all the operands are true. For more than two operands, the objects are nested from the left, <computeroutput>(a and b) and c</computeroutput>, and the expression formatter writes them as a single chain, <computeroutput>(a and b and c)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>All the operands are evaluated before the check, so, unlike the standard algorithm of the same name, the function does not stop at the first operand that is false.</para>
<para>The name is the same as that of <computeroutput>std::all_of</computeroutput>: after a <computeroutput>using namespace std</computeroutput>, an unqualified call with three or more operands of the same type selects the standard algorithm, so the function must be called as <computeroutput>mt::all_of()</computeroutput>. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
