<simplesect kind="par"><title>Constraints</title><para>Enabled only if each operand satisfies <computeroutput><ref refid="conceptmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1extension_1_1checkable" kindref="compound">extension::checkable</ref></computeroutput>, as for <computeroutput>expect()</computeroutput>. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>An object that evaluates to true if at least one of the operand expressions is true, including when all are.</para>
</simplesect>
The <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-logical-functions_1gadc2224d07a9bf118c8772518a7d3c4fd" kindref="member">any_of</ref></computeroutput> function template provides a generic logical disjunction for any expression types. It constructs a <computeroutput><ref refid="structmicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail_1_1or__op" kindref="compound">detail::or_op</ref></computeroutput> logical disjunction object, which evaluates to <computeroutput>true</computeroutput> if at least one of the operands is true; the disjunction is inclusive, so the result is also true when all the conditions are true. For more than two operands, the objects are nested from the left, and the expression formatter writes them as a single chain, <computeroutput>(a or b or c)</computeroutput>.</para>
<para>All the operands are evaluated before the check, so the function does not stop at the first operand that is true; and, as for <computeroutput><ref refid="group__micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-cpp-api-logical-functions_1ga0a385c59a2f7d3c4cfef77d2d3b4f3d6" kindref="member">all_of()</ref></computeroutput>, it must be called as <computeroutput>mt::any_of()</computeroutput> after a <computeroutput>using namespace std</computeroutput>. </para>
